--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INTRODUCTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MaxGPA is a web application for University of Oregon students who want to plan
their degree strategically. It shows the historical grade distributions for
every required course in a major — broken down by instructor — so students can
identify which sections offer the best outcomes and build a realistic course
plan before registration opens.

The system also includes an Admin portal for staff to load and update grade
data and degree requirement information.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INTERFACE OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The app has three main pages, accessible from the navigation bar at the top:

  Degree Planner     The main planning workspace (default page)
  My Degree Plan     View and export plans you have saved
  Admin              Staff portal for uploading data

On the Degree Planner page, the screen is divided into three regions:

  LEFT SIDEBAR
    Contains four filters: Major, Year, Course Search, and Instructor.
    Changes here immediately update the courses shown in the main area.

  TOP PANEL (Requirements Checklist)
    Appears after you select a major. Shows every required course group
    with badges that turn green as you add courses to your plan. Your
    current plan (course list, avg GPA, action buttons) sits on the right
    side of this panel.

  MAIN AREA (Course Cards)
    One card per course. Each card shows a grade distribution chart and,
    when expanded, a ranked list of instructors with their average GPAs.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STUDENT TASKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TASK 1: Select your major and see which courses are required
------------------------------------------------------------

Goal: Scope the planner to your degree program so you can see exactly which
courses you need.

  1. In the left sidebar, find the "Major" section.
  2. Click the radio button next to your major:
       Computer Science / Mathematics / Business Administration
  3. The Requirements Checklist panel appears at the top of the main area.
     It lists every required course group for that major with grey badges
     for each course — these will turn green as you add courses to your plan.

If no Requirements Checklist appears, the degree plan for your major has not
been loaded. Contact your system administrator.


TASK 2: Choose which years of grade data to include
----------------------------------------------------

Goal: Narrow the data to a specific time window — useful if you want to see
only recent instructors or compare trends across years.

  1. In the left sidebar, find the "Year" section.
  2. Check one or more academic year boxes (e.g., AY24, AY25, AY26).
     AY26 = the academic year running Fall 2025 through Summer 2026.
  3. Course cards in the main area update immediately to reflect only
     sections taught during the selected years.

  NOTE: At least one year must be selected for courses to appear.
  If the main area is empty, check that you have at least one year selected.

  TIP: Selecting more years gives a broader picture of each instructor's
  history. Selecting fewer years shows only recent data.


TASK 3: Find the best instructor for a required course
------------------------------------------------------

Goal: Identify which instructor section of a required course has historically
given the highest grades, so you can prioritize registering for that section.

  1. In the main area, find the course card for the course you are
     researching (e.g., "CS 313 — Interm Data Structures").
     Required courses appear at the top of the list, sorted by requirement
     group.
  2. Click anywhere on the card to expand it.
  3. A ranked list of instructors appears, sorted by average GPA (highest
     first). Each row shows:
       - Instructor name
       - Average GPA awarded in that course
       - Grade distribution bar (A / B / C / DNF)
  4. Review the list. The instructor at the top has the highest historical
     average GPA for that course.

  TIP: Use the "Instructor" filter in the left sidebar to show only sections
  taught by a specific instructor across all courses.


TASK 4: Add a course to your plan
----------------------------------

Goal: Record your chosen instructor for a course so the system can track
your progress toward completing all requirements.

  1. Expand the course card (see Task 3).
  2. Find the instructor row you want.
  3. Click the "+ Add" button on that row.
  4. The course is added to "Your Plan" on the right side of the Requirements
     Checklist. The badge for that course in the checklist turns green.

To swap to a different instructor after adding:
  - Expand the same course card. Other instructor rows will now show a
    "Swap" button instead of "+ Add". Click Swap to replace your selection.
  - OR: if the amber "Better options available" panel appears in the
    Requirements Checklist, click "Swap" next to any suggested upgrade,
    or "Swap All" to apply every suggestion at once.

To remove a course from your plan:
  - In the Requirements Checklist, find the course in "Your Plan" and
    click the X button on its row.


TASK 5: Generate an optimal plan automatically
----------------------------------------------

Goal: Let the system build a complete plan for you by selecting the
highest-GPA instructor for each required course.

  1. Make sure you have selected a major (Task 1) and at least one year
     (Task 2).
  2. In the Requirements Checklist panel, click "Generate Plan"
     (the purple button with a sparkle icon).
  3. The system fetches the best available instructor for every required
     course and fills in Your Plan automatically.

  NOTE: Any courses you have already added manually are preserved.
  Generate Plan only fills in the courses you have not yet selected.

  TIP: After generating, review the plan and use Swap (Task 4) to override
  any auto-selected instructor with your own preference.


TASK 6: Save your completed plan
---------------------------------

Goal: Permanently store your plan so you can refer back to it later or
export it to PDF.

  1. Add courses until every section in the Requirements Checklist shows a
     green checkmark. The progress indicator at the top of the checklist
     shows "X/Y sections complete".
  2. Once all sections are complete, the "Save Plan" button (green, with a
     save icon) becomes active.
  3. Click "Save Plan".
  4. A dialog appears with a suggested plan name (e.g.,
     "Computer Science — May 4, 2026"). Edit the name if you like.
  5. Click "Save". The plan is saved to My Degree Plan and your current
     draft is cleared.

  NOTE: The Save Plan button remains disabled until every requirement group
  is satisfied. See the checklist to identify which groups still need courses.

  TIP: You can also click "Clear" to remove all courses from your current
  draft and start over without saving.


TASK 7: View and export a saved plan to PDF
--------------------------------------------

Goal: Review a saved plan and download it as a PDF to print or share with
an advisor.

  1. Click "My Degree Plan" in the top navigation bar.
  2. Your saved plans are listed, newest first. Each card shows the plan
     name, the courses and instructors selected, and the average GPA.
  3. To export a plan as a PDF:
       a. Find the plan card you want to export.
       b. Click the "Export PDF" button on that card.
       c. The browser downloads a PDF file named after your plan.
  4. To delete a plan you no longer need, click the "Delete" button on
     that card. This action cannot be undone.

  TIP: For best PDF quality, use Google Chrome. If the exported PDF appears
  blank or cut off, try zooming out in your browser before exporting.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADMIN TASKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Access the Admin portal by clicking "Admin" in the top navigation bar.
No login is required.

The Admin page has two main sections:
  Import Grade Data       Load a new grade-history CSV from the university
  Degree Requirements     Load or edit degree requirement plans by major


TASK 8: Upload new grade-history data
--------------------------------------

Goal: Replace the grade-history data in the system with an updated CSV file
obtained from the university.

  1. Go to the Admin page and find the "Import Grade Data" section.
  2. Drag your grade-history CSV file onto the upload area, or click the
     area to open a file picker.
     The CSV must contain at minimum these columns:
       TERM, TERM_DESC, SUBJ, NUMB, CRN, INSTRUCTOR
       and grade count columns (AP, A, AM, BP, B, ... F, P, N, OTHER, W, TOT_NON_W)
  3. A preview appears showing the first valid data row from the file.
     Confirm that the fields look correct (e.g., TERM: 202601, SUBJ: CS,
     NUMB: 313, INSTRUCTOR: Smith).
  4. Click "Confirm & Import" to load the data.
     The system reports how many rows were inserted and which terms were
     updated vs. newly added.
  5. Click "Upload another file" to load an additional CSV, or navigate
     away when done.

  NOTE: If the file contains terms already in the system, those terms are
  replaced entirely. This allows corrections and updates to be re-uploaded
  without creating duplicate records.

  NOTE: The reconciliation rules in data/meta/Reconciliation.csv are applied
  automatically during import to normalize course numbers and titles.


TASK 9: Import a degree plan for a major
-----------------------------------------

Goal: Replace all degree requirements for one major by uploading a
structured CSV file.

  1. Go to the Admin page and find the "Degree Requirements" section.
  2. Click the major tab for the major you want to update:
       Computer Science / Mathematics / Business Administration
  3. In the "{Major} Requirements" card, drag your degree-plan CSV onto
     the upload area, or click to browse.
     Required CSV columns: GROUP, GROUP_TYPE, SUBJ, NUMB
     Optional columns: SEQ (sequence tag), TITLE (course title)

     Example row:
       Upper-Division Core, all, CS, 315,, Intermed Algorithms

  4. A preview appears showing the total number of courses found and the
     first valid row. Confirm the fields look correct.
  5. Click "Confirm & Import".

  WARNING: This replaces ALL existing requirement groups and courses for
  the selected major. The operation cannot be undone from the UI.

  See data/dummy_data/dummy_degree_plan.csv for a correctly formatted
  example file.


TASK 10: Manually edit requirement groups
------------------------------------------

Goal: Add or remove individual courses or groups from a major's requirements
without uploading a full CSV.

  1. Go to the Admin page and find the "Degree Requirements" section.
  2. Click the major tab for the major you want to edit.
  3. Below the CSV upload card, the "{Major} Requirements" list shows all
     current requirement groups. Click a group header to expand it.

  To remove a course from a group:
    Click "Remove" on the right side of the course row.

  To add a course to a group:
    a. Expand the group.
    b. Click "+ Add course to this group" at the bottom of the group.
    c. Select a subject from the dropdown (CS, MATH, or BA).
    d. Select a course from the course dropdown.
    e. If the group type is "one sequence", enter the sequence tag
       (A, B, or C) in the Seq field.
    f. Click "Add".

  To delete an entire group:
    Click "Delete group" in the group header. This removes the group and
    all courses within it.

  To add a new requirement group:
    a. Scroll to the bottom of the requirements list.
    b. In the "Add Requirement Group" form, enter a group name
       (e.g., "Upper-Division Elective").
    c. Select the group type:
         All required          — student must take every course in the group
         Choose at least one   — student must take at least one course
         Choose one sequence   — student must complete one full sub-sequence
    d. Click "Add Group".
    e. Expand the new group and add courses to it (see steps above).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TROUBLESHOOTING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No courses appear in the main area
  - Make sure at least one year is checked in the Year filter (left sidebar).
  - Make sure a major is selected.

The "Save Plan" button is greyed out
  - Not all requirement sections are complete. Look at the Requirements
    Checklist and find any groups that still show grey badges. Add a course
    from each incomplete group.

A required course is not showing up in the main area
  - The course may not have been offered in the selected year(s). Try
    selecting additional years to broaden the data range.

The grade data looks outdated
  - Ask your administrator to upload a new grade-history CSV (Task 8).

The requirements shown don't match the current UO Catalog
  - Ask your administrator to import an updated degree plan CSV (Task 9).

The PDF export downloads as a blank file
  - Try using Google Chrome. Other browsers may handle canvas rendering
    differently. Also check that the plan card is fully visible on screen
    before clicking Export PDF.

The app does not load or shows a connection error
  - Both the frontend (port 3000) and backend API (port 8000) must be
    running. Refer to the Installation Instructions for how to start them.

